/-!
# Admissible floor sections of a trivial surface adjoint extend

Let `(S, B)` be a `ℚ`-factorial projective dlt pair on a complex surface, with `B` an effective
`ℚ`-divisor and `K_S + B ∼_ℚ 0`. Every component `C_P` of the reduced floor `⌊B⌋` is a normal
curve and carries the adjunction pair `(C_P, B_{C_P})`, `B_{C_P} = Diff_{C_P}(B - C_P)`. Then in
every sufficiently divisible even degree `m`, every admissible section system
`(t_P) ∈ ⊕_P H⁰(C_P, m(K_{C_P} + B_{C_P}))` on the finite collection of these curves — compatible
under every crepant birational map between the curves and between their point strata — is the
system of Poincaré residues of one section `s ∈ H⁰(S, m(K_S + B))`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_isPoincareResidue_of_mem_admissibleSections`: the extension of admissible
  floor section systems from the components of `⌊B⌋` to `S`.

## Implementation notes

The components of `⌊B⌋` are indexed by the prime divisors `P` of `S` with `⌊coeff_P B⌋ ≠ 0`;
for each such `P` the curve `C_P`, its closed immersion `j_P : C_P ⟶ S` onto `P` and the
different `B_{C_P}` form an adjunction step (`MMP.Fourfold.IsAdjunctionStep`). Since the floor
components of a dlt surface are normal, `C_P` is the normalization of `P`. Admissibility is
`MMP.Fourfold.admissibleSections` for a residue restriction structure
`MMP.Fourfold.ResidueRestriction` on the collection `(C_P, B_{C_P})` in degree `m`, and the
extension `s` restricts to `t_P` in the sense of `MMP.Fourfold.IsPoincareResidue` along `j_P`.

## References

* [J. Kollár et al., *Flips and abundance for algebraic threefolds*][KollarFlips]
-/

